# ludic.tactics - what makes a shooter's enemy look smart, as data and pure functions: graded perception (a cone, range,
# light, line of sight through a port, hearing, memory, five alert states), cover points generated by rays and picked by
# scores with reservations, a utility scorer over archetype rows, morale and suppression, a fair aim-error model, and
# squads that share a contact, hand out roles and say callouts. Uses ludic.base and nothing else. See README.md.
package "ludic.tactics"
version "0.1.0"
kind source
